{% doc %}
  Emits the site-wide Organization JSON-LD node.

  Rendered only from `structured-data.liquid`, and only on the homepage, so the
  store has exactly one Organization node rather than one per page.

  The `@id` is stable across environments because it is derived from `shop.url`
  (the canonical primary domain) rather than `request.origin`. On a preview theme
  or a `*.myshopify.com` host, `request.origin` differs, which would mint a second
  identifier for the same entity.

  Deliberately omitted: `address`, `telephone`, and any email. This repo is public
  and the operation is home-based, so postal and contact detail must not appear
  here. Organization markup invites "completing" the node with an address; do not.
  See the Sensitive Content section of CLAUDE.md.

  `sameAs` must list real brand profile URLs only. A bare platform homepage
  (`https://www.facebook.com`) asserts that this Organization is that platform,
  which is a false entity claim. Blank settings are skipped, so is any URL with
  no path segment past the host, and the array is omitted entirely when nothing
  survives both tests. That second test is the same one
  `snippets/social-links.liquid` applies before rendering a link, so this array
  and the visible links stay the same set. `social_keys` below duplicates that
  snippet's platform list; adding a platform means editing both.

  The `logo` ImageObject carries no `width` / `height`. Deriving them means
  dividing by `settings.logo.aspect_ratio`, and an SVG can report that as zero or
  nil. Liquid renders a divide-by-zero as an error string, which would land inside
  this script tag and silently invalidate the whole node. Google does not require
  the dimensions, so the safe move is to omit them rather than guard the divide.
  Google does require a raster logo of at least 112x112; SVG is not reliably
  consumed, so keep the logo setting on a PNG.

  `hasMerchantReturnPolicy` is hardcoded, and deliberately not a theme setting.
  The return-policy categories are not one-field swaps:
  `MerchantReturnFiniteReturnWindow` additionally requires `merchantReturnDays`,
  and Google wants `returnFees`, `returnMethod`, and `refundType`. A dropdown
  would let the operator pick a category that renders a structurally invalid
  node, with nothing in CI to catch it (`shopify theme check` does not parse
  JSON-LD, and `seo-review:test` is unit tests only). It is also a
  legal-adjacent claim that has to track `/policies/refund-policy`, and a
  theme-editor dropdown can drift from that policy silently. Changing it should
  cost a code edit and a release note. Before changing the category, check
  Google's required fields for the new one.

  KNOWN AND ACCEPTED: this node asserts a 14-day return window store-wide, and
  the published policy's exclusion list (custom or personalized designs, final
  sale, gift cards) covers five of the six products. Google's org-level node is
  meant for a policy applying to most or all products; here it applies to one.
  This is a chosen trade, not an oversight: `merchantReturnLink` points at the
  live policy that enumerates every exclusion. Do not file the contradiction as
  a bug. The per-product override is closed, not merely unimplemented: Google's
  override path is a `MerchantReturnPolicy` nested under `Offer`, Shopify's
  `structured_data` filter owns that node and emits
  `"@id": "/products/handle?variant=N#offer"`, and shadowing that `@id` to merge
  a property in would mean reproducing Shopify's exact relative id including the
  variant parameter, on products with hundreds of variants, relying on
  undocumented node-merge behaviour. That is the silent-invalidity class the
  structured-data rules in `docs/structured-data.md` exist to prevent.

  `applicableCountry` is the literal `"US"`. Not from
  `localization.available_countries`, which is market config that would silently
  widen a legal claim the day international markets are enabled, and not from
  `shop.address`, because the postal-detail ban above applies and pulling a
  country code out of that object invites the next reader to pull the rest.

  @example
    {% render 'structured-data-organization' %}
{% enddoc %}

{%- liquid
  assign social_keys = 'social_facebook_link,social_instagram_link,social_tiktok_link,social_youtube_link,social_pinterest_link' | split: ','
  assign same_as_urls = ''

  for key in social_keys
    assign social_url = settings[key]
    if social_url != blank
      # Same has-a-profile-path test `snippets/social-links.liquid` applies before it will
      # render a link, so the emitted set matches what the storefront shows. Without it a
      # bare platform homepage renders nowhere yet still asserts the entity claim this
      # snippet's doc block prohibits.
      assign social_path_parts = social_url | split: '//' | last | split: '/'
      if social_path_parts.size > 1 and social_path_parts[1] != ''
        if same_as_urls == blank
          assign same_as_urls = social_url
        else
          assign same_as_urls = same_as_urls | append: '|' | append: social_url
        endif
      endif
    endif
  endfor

  assign org_id = shop.url | append: '/#organization'
  assign org_description = shop.description | default: shop.name

  assign return_policy_id = shop.url | append: '/#return-policy'
  assign return_policy_url = ''
  if shop.refund_policy.url != blank
    assign return_policy_url = shop.url | append: shop.refund_policy.url
  endif
-%}

<script type="application/ld+json">
  {
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@type": "Organization",
    "@id": {{ org_id | json }},
    "name": {{ shop.name | json }},
    "url": {{ shop.url | json }},
    "description": {{ org_description | json }}
    {%- if settings.logo != blank -%}
      ,
      "logo": {
        "@type": "ImageObject",
        "url": {{ settings.logo | image_url: width: 500 | prepend: 'https:' | json }}
      }
    {%- endif -%}
    {%- if same_as_urls != blank -%}
      ,
      "sameAs": [
        {%- assign same_as_list = same_as_urls | split: '|' -%}
        {%- for social_url in same_as_list -%}
          {{ social_url | json }}{%- unless forloop.last -%},{%- endunless -%}
        {%- endfor -%}
      ]
    {%- endif -%}
    ,
    "hasMerchantReturnPolicy": {
      "@type": "MerchantReturnPolicy",
      "@id": {{ return_policy_id | json }},
      "applicableCountry": "US",
      "returnPolicyCategory": "https://schema.org/MerchantReturnFiniteReturnWindow",
      "merchantReturnDays": 14,
      "returnMethod": "https://schema.org/ReturnByMail",
      "returnFees": "https://schema.org/ReturnFeesCustomerResponsibility",
      "refundType": "https://schema.org/FullRefund"
      {%- if return_policy_url != blank -%}
        ,
        "merchantReturnLink": {{ return_policy_url | json }}
      {%- endif -%}
    }
  }
</script>
